{%- comment -%}
  Authorization policy: admin_only (Layer-2, app-owned; spec §12.2, §5.1).
  Permits the tool only when the resolved PRINCIPAL holds the mcp.admin permission
  (user-module RBAC: role mcp_operator, or superadmin). In on_behalf_of delegation the
  check is against the principal (the human), never the agent (§9.4), so an agent can
  never elevate itself.
  Fail-closed: no profile or no permission → deny.
  Contract: return { allow, reason }. Receives principal, agent, arguments, tool,
  delegation_mode.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function is_admin = 'modules/mcp/queries/principal/can', principal: principal, do: 'mcp.admin'
  assign r = {}
  assign r['allow'] = is_admin
  if is_admin
    assign r['reason'] = 'admin'
  else
    assign r['reason'] = 'not_admin'
  endif
  return r
%}
